{:id "0010-dev-seed"
 :title "Dev seed: a signed-in human, their agent, and a first conversation on the emulators"
 :lupa/deps #{"0005-worker"}
 :lupa/area :dev
 :lupa/risk :low
 :goal "One command fills running emulators with what a developer needs to
        try the app: an Auth emulator user whose uid is \"ben\" and who can
        sign in with an email and password, the matching human member, his
        agent \"scout\", and a conversation \"first\" between them. Safe to run
        twice."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/dev/seed.clj" "src/halfahead/worker/store.clj"
         "test/halfahead/dev/seed_test.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/store_test.clj"]
 :design "halfahead.worker.store gains two public writers alongside the
          existing ones, same style and the same demo- guard:
            (write-member! cfg member) and (write-conversation! cfg c)

          halfahead.dev.seed (Babashka):
            (plan {:now inst :email s :password s}) -> pure: a map of
              {:auth-user {...} :members [...] :conversations [...]} with
              valid domain maps (ben: human \"Ben\"; scout: agent \"Scout\"
              owned by ben; conversation \"first\", title \"First light\",
              member-ids [\"ben\" \"scout\"], created-by ben)
            (auth-user-request plan-auth-user) -> pure: the request map for
              the Auth emulator's create-account endpoint
              POST http://<FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST or 127.0.0.1:9099>
              /identitytoolkit.googleapis.com/v1/projects/demo-halfahead/accounts
              with \"Authorization: Bearer owner\" and JSON
              {localId \"ben\", email, password, displayName \"Ben\"}
            (-main & args) -> runs the plan: creates the auth user (an
              EMAIL_EXISTS or DUPLICATE_LOCAL_ID error counts as done), then
              upserts members and conversations through store. Defaults:
              email ben@halfahead.test, password from env HALFAHEAD_DEV_PASSWORD
              or \"halfahead-dev\". Prints what it did.
          Never touches a non-demo project (store already refuses)."
 :acceptance
 ["plan returns valid :ha/member and :ha/conversation maps (assert with
   halfahead.schema/valid?) and the agent's owner-id is \"ben\""
  "auth-user-request builds the URL, header, and body exactly as above,
   honouring FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST when given (pass env in as an
   argument so the test is pure)"
  "write-member! and write-conversation! build PATCH requests to
   members/<id> and conversations/<id> (assert via store's :send-fn) and
   refuse a non-demo project"
  "-main treats an EMAIL_EXISTS response from the auth endpoint as success
   (test with an injected send function)"
  "`bb test` stays green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Do not edit bb.edn (run it as `bb -m halfahead.dev.seed`), the schema,
   worker.main, or worker.engine"
  "No messages in the seed; no real project; no secrets committed"]
 :context ["src/halfahead/worker/store.clj" "test/halfahead/worker/store_test.clj"
           "docs/SCHEMA.md" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
